        "content": "{\"formal\": {\"statement\": \"∀ (IsQualifying : Set ℤ → Prop)\\n    (IsQualifying_def : ∀ S, IsQualifying S ↔\\n      (∀ n ∈ S, 0 < n) ∧\\n      2 ∈ S ∧\\n      (∀ n > 0, n ^ 2 ∈ S → n ∈ S) ∧\\n      (∀ n ∈ S, (n + 5) ^ 2 ∈ S))\\n    (S : Set ℤ)\\n    (hS : IsLeast IsQualifying S), Sᶜ ∩ {n | 0 < n} = putnam_2017_a1_solution\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"supporting_declarations\": [{\"name\": \"putnam_2017_a1_solution\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"type\": \"Set ℤ\", \"value\": \"@(@(({x : ℤ | x > 0 ∧ (x = 1 ∨ 6 ∣ x)})))\", \"scopes\": []}], \"rendered\": \"∀ (IsQualifying : ((Set ℤ) → Prop)),\\n  ((∀ (S : (Set ℤ)),\\n      ((IsQualifying S) ↔\\n        ((∀ n ∈ S, (0 < n)) ∧ ((2 ∈ S) ∧ ((∀ n > 0, (((n ^ 2) ∈ S) → (n ∈ S))) ∧ (∀ n ∈ S, (((n + 5) ^ 2) ∈ S))))))) →\\n    (∀ (S : (Set ℤ)), ((IsLeast IsQualifying S) → ((Sᶜ ∩ {n | (0 < n)}) = putnam_2017_a1_solution))))\"}, \"signature\": \"(IsQualifying : Set ℤ → Prop)\\n    (IsQualifying_def : ∀ S, IsQualifying S ↔\\n      (∀ n ∈ S, 0 < n) ∧\\n      2 ∈ S ∧\\n      (∀ n > 0, n ^ 2 ∈ S → n ∈ S) ∧\\n      (∀ n ∈ S, (n + 5) ^ 2 ∈ S))\\n    (S : Set ℤ)\\n    (hS : IsLeast IsQualifying S) :\\n    Sᶜ ∩ {n | 0 < n} = putnam_2017_a1_solution\", \"informal\": \"Let $S$ be the smallest set of positive integers such that (a) $2$ is in $S$, (b) $n$ is in $S$ whenever $n^2$ is in $S$, and (c) $(n+5)^2$ is in $S$ whenever $n$ is in $S$. Which positive integers are not in $S$?.\", \"docstring\": \"/--\\nLet $S$ be the smallest set of positive integers such that (a) $2$ is in $S$, (b) $n$ is in $S$ whenever $n^2$ is in $S$, and (c) $(n+5)^2$ is in $S$ whenever $n$ is in $S$. Which positive integers are not in $S$?.\\n-/\", \"prechecks\": {\"status\": \"completed\", \"hints\": [], \"vacuity\": \"unresolved\"}, \"advisory\": {\"paraphrase_status\": \"completed\", \"differences\": [\"The paraphrase introduces the IsQualifying predicate, which is not present in the informal problem.\", \"The paraphrase uses formal logic quantifiers, while the informal problem is more conversational.\", \"The paraphrase includes 'putnam_2017_a1_solution,' which is not mentioned in the informal problem.\", \"The paraphrase refers to the complement of S, while the informal problem explicitly asks about the complement.\", \"The paraphrase mentions 'for every S' in a different context than the informal problem.\"], \"paraphrase\": \"For every IsQualifying predicate, for every set S, if IsQualifying S holds, then for every S, if S is the least set satisfying IsQualifying, the intersection of the complement of S with the set of positive integers equals putnam_2017_a1_solution.\", \"comparison_status\": \"completed\"}}"
